        "geology": "The Scheldt estuary as we know it now is only formed 700 years ago, when mayor flood connected the Easter and Westerscheldt . The latter would become the only entry of the Scheldt. The river it self dates from a much older period (Pliocene).",
        "hydrology": "The Scheldt is rain fed river with a macro tidal estuary (maximum tidal amplitude 5.4 m). The tidal influence is stopped by the sluices near Gent, two tributaries remain under tidal influence (Durme and Rupel).",
        "soils": null,
        "vegetation": "tidal marsh (salt-brackish-fresh)"
      },
